        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "63d0cff4-2652-5958-b9d0-451fd6b30020",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eardwulf of Northumbria, Æthelred I of Northumbria, Æthelwald Moll, Æthelthryth, Alhred\n- Places: Northumbria\n- Topics: kingship, dynastic strife, assassination attempts, reigns\n\nFacts:\n- Æthelred I of Northumbria was born around 762 and died on 18 April 796.\n- Æthelred I of Northumbria was the son of Æthelwald Moll and Æthelthryth.\n- Æthelred I of Northumbria possibly became king while still a child after Alhred was deposed.\n- Æthelred I of Northumbria ruled Northumbria from 774 to 779.\n- In 790, Æthelred I of Northumbria again became king of Northumbria.\n- In 790, Northumbria was marked by dynastic strife among several noble families, and Æthelred I of Northumbria attempted to have Eardwulf of Northumbria assassinated.\n- Æthelred I of Northumbria ruled until he was murdered in 796.\n- Eardwulf of Northumbria may have had a second reign from 808 until perhaps 811 or 830.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
